{"title":"2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The height of a stack of identical newspapers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd2999cbedcc3226b1b4cffaa5e6aec462529f91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50 \\text{cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />. Half of the newspapers are removed from the stack. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d129a7b3c0bf9fbd0693afdd426a66d2a0a8c3ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of those removed are put back onto the stack. What is the height of the stack now?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/8/3981c26580d9e65f39e4560e3d17c09d68851706.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 10 \\text{ cm} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 25 \\text{ cm} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 30 \\text{ cm} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 35 \\text{ cm} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 40 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"530\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since half of the news papers are removed from the stack, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/0/950c41de2ec553859947061bc4d870245bcc7e07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50 \\text{ cm} \\times \\frac{1}{2} = 25 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"151\" height=\"38\" /> are removed and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88b007fbfe8b4183da4d308f6e0f4a3c3b028ea7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> are still in the stack. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d129a7b3c0bf9fbd0693afdd426a66d2a0a8c3ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88b007fbfe8b4183da4d308f6e0f4a3c3b028ea7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> removed are put back onto the stack, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/530a6d411166475a658b77d8df9f52a0b420f0c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> are put back in. The height of the stack is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1deb805375bbf17540c649c481f4a9adc21783d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 + 5 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 30 \\text{ cm}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"167\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not